          "title": "You'll want to know: поэт",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "поэт (poét) — \"a poet\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Этот поэт писал о любви и природе. Étot poét pisál o lyubví i priróde. This poet wrote about love and nature."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Masculine; feminine поэтесса, though many women prefer поэт (poét)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "поэт (poét) was borrowed through German Poet from Latin poēta, which comes from Greek poiētḗs 'a maker, a poet' (EtymDB)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
